<title>EGYPT: Egyptian yr/yr inflation down to 4.8 pct in June.</title>
<headline>Egyptian yr/yr inflation down to 4.8 pct in June.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egyptian year-on-year inflation fell to 4.8 percent in June, from 4.9 percent in May and 8.3 percent in June 1996, according to figures from the government's statistics office, available on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The consumer price index for urban areas, set at a base of 100 in the financial year 1986/7, fell 0.1 percent in June, to 383.2 from 383.0 in May 1997, they said. The index stood at 365.8 at the end of June 1996.</p>
<p>				   JUNE 97	 MAY 97    JUNE 96</p>
<p>    Month-on-month		+0.1	  +0.5	  +0.2</p>
<p>    Year-on-year		  +4.8	  +4.9	  +8.3</p>
<p>    INDEX (base 1986/7)	 383.2	 383.0	 365.8</p>
<p>-- Esmat Salaheddin +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
